  "rootCause": {
    "primary": "v3 ref_audio synthesis can stochastically generate long near-silent audio for individual chunks. The previous retry path repeated essentially the same generation configuration, so some retries reproduced the same 18-24 second silence and created very large retry overhead.",
    "contributingFactors": [
      "The v3 batch path used a 300-frame decode cap for every first attempt. Broken ref_audio rows could run near the full cap and return 15-24 seconds of mostly silence.",
      "Retry attempts were per chunk, not whole batch, but they reused the same sampler/config for ref_audio and could fail repeatedly.",
      "Reference audio encoding was not safely cached in the Voice API resolve path, so repeated requests/retries could redo reference preprocessing.",
      "The issue is not AutoNews, not Whisper alignment, and not batch-size persistence. Batch 19 was received by the backend. Built-in voices are much less affected, but severe silent attempts can still happen stochastically and are still caught by existing QA."
    ],
    "notRootCause": ["AutoNews pipeline overhead", "Whisper alignment causing TTS silence", "Fallback to v2", "Batch size UI not persisted", "Retrying whole batches"]
  },
  "codeChanges": [
    {"file": "D:\\VieNeu-TTS\\apps\\voice_clone_api.py", "lines": "146, 1060-1087", "change": "Added a ref_audio reference-code cache keyed by resolved path, mtime_ns, and file size. The resolved voice now carries refAudioCache metadata."},
    {"file": "D:\\VieNeu-TTS\\apps\\voice_clone_api.py", "lines": "1093-1155, 1486-1551, 1850, 2156", "change": "Added ref_audio retry variants. Silence/volume retries for ref_audio now shift sampler parameters and apply a text-based max_new_frames cap instead of repeating the identical failed configuration."},
    {"file": "D:\\VieNeu-TTS\\apps\\voice_clone_api.py", "lines": "1103-1106, 2059-2085, 2222", "change": "Applied a ref_audio-specific frame cap to v3 batch generation and reported maxNewFrames/refAudioFrameCapApplied/refAudioOptimization in timings. Built-in preset voices keep the existing 300-frame first-pass cap."}
